--- !u!114 &509982333
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 509982330}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "<size=70><color=#2ECC71><b>QUICK START GUIDE</b></size></color>\r\n\r\n<size=40><b>GUESS
    THE GOOD WORD, AVOID THE BAD</b></size>\r\n<size=35>\r\n1. To quickly start playing,
    draw a card from the deck and hold it so that only you can see the front.\r\n\r\n2.
    Then, you give a <b><color=#DBB26F>ONE WORD</b></color> hint to someone. This
    hint should help that other player think of the <color=#2ECC71><b>GOOD</b></color>
    word, found in the top, green section of the card.\r\n\r\n3. Once the other player
    thinks of a guess, they respond back to you with their <b><color=#DBB26F>ONE
    WORD</b></color> guess.\r\nIf that guess is the <color=#E74C3C><b>BAD</b></color>
    word, found in the bottom, red section of the card, you lose!\r\nIf that guess
    is neither the <color=#2ECC71><b>GOOD</b></color> word nor the <color=#E74C3C><b>BAD</b></color>
    word, then you give another <b><color=#DBB26F>ONE WORD</b></color> hint and they
    get to guess again.\r\nIf they guess the <color=#2ECC71><b>GOOD</b></color> word,
    then you\u2019ve won!\r\n\r\n4. Draw a new card and keep playing, or try a new
    way to play!\r\n</size>\r\n\r\n<size=70><color=#E74C3C><b>HOW TO PLAY</b></size></color>\r\n\r\n<size=40><b>TAKING
    A TURN</b></size>\r\n\r\n<size=35>1. Play begins with a <b><color=#DBB26F>HINTER</b></color>
    drawing a card from the deck and giving the first clue.\r\n\r\n2. The <b><color=#DBB26F>GUESSER</b></color>
    (or <b><color=#DBB26F>GUESSERS</b></color>) then respond with what they think
    is the <color=#2ECC71><b>GOOD</b></color> word.\r\n\r\n\u2022 On each person\u2019s
    turn, they <b>MUST</b> make a reasonable attempt and give a word.\r\n\u2022 <b><color=#DBB26F>GUESSERS</b></color>
    can only say any given word once per round; if they mistakenly repeat a word,
    alert them to make a new guess.\r\n\r\n3. This process repeats, with the <b>HINTER</b>
    giving a hint, then the <b>GUESSER</b> giving a guess, until either the <color=#2ECC71><b>GOOD</b></color>
    word or the <color=#E74C3C><b>BAD</b></color> word is spoken.\r\nThen the current
    card is discarded and a new one is drawn to continue the game.</size>\r\n\r\n\r\n<size=40><b>GETTING
    POINTS</b></size>\r\n\r\n<size=35>\u2022 When a <b><color=#DBB26F>GUESSER</b></color>
    successfully identifies the <color=#2ECC71><b>GOOD</b></color> word, their team
    gains a point.\r\n\u2022 If a <b><color=#DBB26F>GUESSER</b></color> or <b><color=#DBB26F>HINTER</b></color>
    says the <color=#E74C3C><b>BAD</b></color> word, the other team gains a point.</size>\r\n\r\n\r\n<size=40><b>WHAT
    HINTS ARE ALLOWED?</b></size>\r\n\r\n<indent=10>\u2022 The <b><color=#DBB26F>HINTER</b></color>
    can only give a single one-word hint on each of their turns.</indent>\r\n<indent=10>\u2022
    Hints can <b>NOT</b> be proper nouns and can <b>NOT</b> be in other languages.</indent>\r\n<indent=10>\u2022
    Hints can be spelled out to avoid confusion, but you can <b>NOT</b> explain your
    reasoning or give any other additional information (including tone and gestures).</indent>\r\n<indent=10>\u2022
    Unlike the <b><color=#DBB26F>GUESSER</b></color>, the <b><color=#DBB26F>HINTER</b></color>
    may repeat words as much as they like.</indent>\r\n<indent=10>\u2022 <b><color=#DBB26F>HINTERS</b></color>
    may also use words that the <b><color=#DBB26F>GUESSER</b></color> originally
    gave as guesses.</indent>\r\n<indent=10>\u2022 Get creative with your hints!
    Remember, you can only communicate with <b>one word per turn</b>!</indent>\r\n\r\n\r\n<size=70><b><color=#DBB26F>WAYS
    TO PLAY</b></size></color>\r\n\r\n<size=22><b><color=#8AB1D8>*recommended</b></size></color>\r\n<size=40><b>HEAD-TO-HEAD</b><i>
    (4+ players)</i></size>\r\n\r\n<size=35><indent=10>\u2022 Split into two teams,
    then designate one <b><color=#DBB26F>HINTER</b></color> per team.\r\n\u2022 On
    the first turn, flip a coin to see who goes first (\u201CTeam 1\u201D). On following
    turns, alternate which team goes first.\r\n\u2022 In head-to-head, both teams
    are trying to guess the same card.\r\n\u2022 Team 1\u2019s <b><color=#DBB26F>HINTER</b></color>
    gives their hint, and Team 1\u2019s <b><color=#DBB26F>GUESSER(S)</b></color>
    respond.\r\nIf neither the <color=#2ECC71><b>GOOD</b></color> word nor the <color=#E74C3C><b>BAD</b></color>
    word is guessed, continue.\r\n\u2022 Team 2\u2019s <b><color=#DBB26F>HINTER</b></color>
    poses a different hint to their own team, and Team 2\u2019s <b><color=#DBB26F>GUESSER(S)</b></color>
    respond. Then go back to Team 1.\r\n\u2022 Repeat this process until either the
    <color=#2ECC71><b>GOOD</b></color> word or the <color=#E74C3C><b>BAD</b></color>
    word is spoken.\r\n\u2022 After every 2 cards, each team must switch to a new
    <b><color=#DBB26F>HINTER</b></color>.\r\n\u2022 First team to 10 points wins!
    (See <b>GETING POINTS</b>)</size></indent>\r\n\r\n<size=22><b><color=#8AB1D8>*casual</b></size></color>\r\n<size=40><b>FREEPLAY</b><i>
    (2+ players)</i></size>\r\n\r\n<size=35>\u2022 In Freeplay, there is only one
    <b><color=#DBB26F>HINTER</b></color> at a time.\r\n\u2022 If there are only two
    players, the <b><color=#DBB26F>HINTER</b></color> and <b>GUESSER</b> go back
    and forth until the <color=#2ECC71><b>GOOD</b></color> word or <color=#E74C3C><b>BAD</b></color>
    word is said, then switch roles.\r\n\u2022 If there are more than two players,
    <b><color=#DBB26F>GUESSERS</b></color> may work together or compete.\r\n\u2022
    If competing, the <b><color=#DBB26F>HINTER</b></color> gives hints individually
    to each <b><color=#DBB26F>GUESSER</b></color>.\r\n\u2022 It is not necessary
    to keep score in Freeplay.</size>"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: ebe42fc41b7ea9d42a485aae452d3285, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 5998946762559453635, guid: ebe42fc41b7ea9d42a485aae452d3285, type: 2}
